%N A394672 Number of n-partite partitions of {n}^n into distinct n-tuples.
%C A394672 Number of factorizations of m^n into distinct factors where m is a product of n distinct primes. a(2) = 5: (2*3)^2 = 36 has 5 factorizations into distinct factors: 36, 3*12, 4*9, 2*18, 2*3*6.
%C A394672 Number of partitions of the multiset with n copies each of 1,2,...,n into distinct blocks. a(2) = 5: 1122, 11|22, 1|122, 112|2, 1|12|2.
%F A394672 a(n) = [(Product_{j=1..n} x_j)^n] 1/2 * Product_{i_1,...,i_n>=0} (1 + Product_{j=1..n} x_j^i_j).
%F A394672 a(n) = A219585(n,n).
%F A394672 a(n) = A045778(A181555(n)) = A045778(A002110(n)^n).
%e A394672 a(2) = 5: [(2,2)], [(2,0),(0,2)], [(2,1),(0,1)], [(1,2),(1,0)], [(1,1),(1,0),(0,1)].
%Y A394672 Main diagonal of A219585.
%Y A394672 Cf. A002110, A045778, A181555, A322488.
%K A394672 nonn,more,new
%O A394672 0,3
